  "payloads": [
    {
      "type": "perf",
      "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "prompt": "The orchestrator filter functions in orchestrator_filters.py use linear search patterns that cause O(n*m) complexity where O(n) is achievable:\n\n1. In filter_file_conflicts: for each eligible task ID, the code does next((t for t in candidate_tasks if t.id == eid), None) to find the task object. This is O(m) per eligible ID.\n\n2. In filter_rollup_conflicts: same linear search pattern for candidate task lookup.\n\n3. In filter_file_conflicts: when building the deferral message, there's another linear scan through active_tasks to find the specific blocking task.\n\nThe fix: pre-build lookup dicts at the top of each filter function. Build candidate_by_id = {t.id: t for t in candidate_tasks} once, then use candidate_by_id.get(eid) for O(1) lookups. Similarly pre-build active task indexes where needed.\n\nThis is a pure performance optimization with no behavior change. Run the backend test suite to verify.\n\nKey files to review or modify:\n- backend/app/orchestrator_filters.py",
      "base_branch": "research/7f5b59a3"
    }
  ],
